For the specific moduli \(t=\ell s\), there is a useful extension of the LV argument. Split the characters according to whether their conductor contains \(\ell\). Those that do have conductor at least \(Y\); the others reduce to LV’s smooth-modulus sum. When \(\log Y\asymp(\log N)^{3/4}\), this recovers the needed sparse-set saving within the inflated-height range. It supplies the progression first moment, but still needs a bound turning relation counts into capped success probabilities.
