I’m consolidating the results. The reduction isolates an averaged capped special-q success estimate, and the inflated design has a route to its progression first moment. The remaining bound must control how that first moment is distributed across fields and targets. None of the verified estimates supplies it, so the proposed \(c<1\) constants remain conditional.
